# Backend Rules

Full contracts: `dev-docs/reference/backend-shared-utilities.md` (one row per module - grep it by helper name), `backend/AGENTS.md` (the rules and an index of `dev-docs/reference/`: `backend-directory-map.md`, `migrations-safety.md`, `backend-testing.md`, `backend-configuration.md`), `backend/app/<area>/AGENTS.md`.

## Conventions

- Async everywhere (SQLAlchemy, Redis, httpx); type hints on every signature; Pydantic models for every API schema; SQLAlchemy 2.0 `Mapped[]` / `mapped_column()`.
- Routes are thin (`api/v1/<resource>.py`, `Depends(get_current_user)` + `get_db`), business logic lives in `services/`; register routers in `main.py`.
- New model: import it in `app/models/__init__.py`, then `uv run python -m alembic -c alembic/alembic.ini revision --autogenerate -m "..."` and harden the migration (below).
- Secrets: `encrypt_value()` / `decrypt_value()` / `decrypt_json()` before any DB write; never in env vars or logs.
- A secret column may hold a vault reference: read it with `reveal_field()` / `reveal_json_field()` (`services/vault`), keep or export it with `decrypt_stored_value()`.
- Log exceptions with `format_exc(e)`, never a raw `%s`. Constant-time compare with `timing_safe_str_eq()`.
- An async hot path awaits `ensure_hot_path_imports()` before importing a heavy module inline.
- Lint `uv run ruff check app/` (`--fix`); tests `make test ARGS="tests/test_<name>.py"` from the repo root (CI runs `-n logical`: deterministic param ids, `tests/scratch_database.py` for PostgreSQL, `tests/app_sources.py` for source tripwires).
- A failing tripwire test means a rule was re-spelled outside its module: move the code to the owner, never patch the tripwire.
- No workarounds in the generic layers (invariant 18, rule 99): no vendor or tool name, no phrase list reading text; the owner declares the property (catalog, adapter, `ToolDefinition`), or the model answers in a structure (`tests/test_no_workarounds.py`).

## Visibility and permissions (the usual non-admin 500)

- Lists: `user_visible_query()`; composable clauses: `user_visible_filter()`; groups from `get_user_group_ids()`. A model queried through them declares `is_company_managed`, `shared_group_ids`, `shared_group_permissions`, `shared_user_ids`, `shared_user_permissions`, `access_restricted` and joins the `CompanyManagedEntity` union. Test as a NON-admin: `is_admin=True` short-circuits the predicate (rule 19, `tests/test_visibility_helpers.py`).
- Callers with no account: `caller_visible_filter()` / `company_wide_visible_filter()`; assignments are visible exactly when their agent is (`assignment_visible_filter()`).
- Edit rights: `can_manage()` (served as `can_manage`); agent / assignment writes: `writable_agent_error()` / `assert_writable_agent()` and the assignment pair; KB content writes: `knowledge_base_write_refusal()`; company-managed toggle: `handle_company_managed_toggle()`.
- Admin reach: REST takes the admin bypass on detail routes, lists take `?scope=` (`EntityListScope`); agent tools use `agent_tool_admin_bypass()`, never the role.
- Path ids: `parse_path_id()` / `parse_conversation_id()` (malformed id = the route's 404); `get_user_*()` helpers already do it.
- Bindings a write adds (tool sources, integrations, channel bots, trigger integration) go through `api/v1/binding_access.py`; what a row already holds is never re-judged.
- Files: `authorize_file_access()` / `load_readable_file()` (`services/file_access.py`) - unreadable answers exactly like unknown (404). Byte responses: `services/file_responses.py`, never a hand-written `Cache-Control`.

## Migrations (mandatory - `dev-docs/reference/migrations-safety.md`)

`--autogenerate` output is NOT safe as-is. Single Alembic head (re-point `down_revision` after a rebase); idempotent (`IF NOT EXISTS`, guarded `DO $$`); lock-light (no rewrites, no `SET NOT NULL` on large tables, NEVER `CONCURRENTLY` - it deadlocks behind the migration lock - indexes via `create_index_in_place()` in an `autocommit_block`); every lock-taking DDL = idempotency probe, then `terminate_lock_holders(conn, "<table>")` + `set_lock_timeout(conn)` from `app.core.migration_ddl`, then the DDL. Never a second migration lock. Verify with `make test ARGS="tests/test_migration_integrity.py"`.

## One rule, one module (reuse, never re-spell)

**`app/core/`**
- `utils.py`: `slugify()`, `parse_delay()`, `safe_uuid()`, `build_content_disposition()` (every download header), `ensure_webhook_secret()` / `strip_webhook_secret()`, `format_exc()`, `chat_processing_key()`, `request_client_ip()` / `client_address()` (the one client-address rule), `strip_null_bytes()` / `sanitize_json_strings()`, `if_none_match_hits()`.
- `security.py`: encryption, `hash_password()` / `verify_password()`, `bcrypt_input()`, `timing_safe_str_eq()` / `timing_safe_header_eq()`, `configured_secret()`, JWT helpers + `JWT_CLOCK_SKEW_LEEWAY`.
- `json_sql.py`: `when_json_parseable()` around every `::jsonb` cast of a `json` column others write. `lone_surrogates.py`: `lone_surrogate_error()` on assignment / flow writes.
- `base_path.py`: `with_base_path()` for redirects and HTML URLs, `route_path(scope)` in path-keyed middleware. `csp.py`: `register_page_policy()` next to a server-rendered template.
- `security_options.py`: `security_option("<key>")` for every security switch; `security_controls.py`: register it in `SECURITY_CONTROLS`. `feature_flags.py`: `is_feature_enabled()` / `require_feature()`.
- `shutdown_finalizers.py`: `start_shutdown_finalizer()` for a write a request cancelled by the graceful shutdown still owes; the lifespan drains it. `track_background_turn()` for agent work outside a request.
- `worker_shutdown.py`: why the worker stops (`cut_cause()`) and the turns it runs; `worker_recycle.py`: the `MAX_REQUESTS` recycle, deferred while a turn runs.
- `migration_ddl.py`, `hot_imports.py`, `redis.py` (`decr_if_positive()` for counter refunds), `log_once.py` (operator notices), `cpu_time.py` (pattern budgets on CPU time), `color.py`, `undeclared_proxy.py` (`forwarded_allow_ips()`), `registration_token.py`, `xtm_auth.py` + `platform_identity.py` + `url_identity.py`, `email_domains.py`, `sso_helpers.py`.

**`app/api/v1/`**
- `helpers.py`: visibility, ownership and write gates above, plus `manual_trigger_refusal()`, `require_run_access()`, `build_mcp_runtime()`, `enqueue_documents()`, `log_kb_activity()`.
- `binding_access.py` (who may add a binding), `agent_import.py` (`create_agent_from_bundle()`, the only import pipeline).

**`app/services/`**
- Gates: `agentic_gate.agentic_refusal()` / `agentic_verdict()` (background work), `ai_hold.py`, `agentic_executions.py`, `integration_credentials.py` (OAuth token sharing), `trigger_integration_access.py`, `company_managed_writes.py`.
- Agent runtime: `builtin_tools/` (every built-in tool builder, `build_identity_context()`, handover peers), `handover_types.py`, `prompt_guard.py` (`build_security_policy()`, `insert_before_safety_anchor()`), `output_format.py`, `assignment_helpers.py`, `persistent_memory.py`, `sub_agent.py` + `sub_agent_files.py`, `delegation.py`, `tool_scaffolding.py`, `context_usage.py`, `tool_tracking.py`.
- Content: `attachment_extract.py` (the one attachment reader), `image_summary.py` (visual summary + colour gate), `schema_guard.py` (untrusted JSON Schema), `vector.py`, `kb_sync_errors.py` / `kb_document_errors.py` (what an error may say).
- Decks and templates: `presentation_spec.py`, `presentations.py`, `presentation_sharing.py` (`apply_sharing()`, the one sharing write), `presentation_pictures.py`, `template_containers.py`, `template_container_seed.py` (`dev-docs/presentations.md`).
- Sharing from an agent tool: `share_principals.py` (`resolve_principals()`, `plan_grants()`, `load_principals()` - people by email / id, groups by name; the write stays `apply_user_share_fields()`).
- Exposure and audit: `resource_exposure.py` / `integration_exposure.py` (read-only), `audit.py` (`log_audit()`, `log_system_audit()`), `agent_deletion.py`, `agent_bundle_projection.py`, `trace_switches.py`, `branding.py`, `email.py` (`render_email()`).

**LLM, tools, integrations, channels**
- `llm/base.py` (`retry_llm_call()`, `build_openai_messages()`, `message_payload_chars()`), `llm/model_capabilities.py`, `llm/router.py` (`build_provider()`, `find_provider_for_model()`), `llm/env_models.py`.
- `tools/agent_loop.py` (loop breaker), `tools/wait_policy.py` (`WAIT_TERMINAL_STATUSES`), `tools/builtin_suites.py`.
- `integrations/http.py` (`AutoRefreshClient`, `safe_request()`, `format_http_error()`, `PLATFORM_USER_AGENT`), `integrations/file_content.py`, `integrations/stale_references.py`.
- Outbound HTTP in routed code: `core/egress.py` `egress_client()` (never a bare `httpx.AsyncClient(`), routes from `services/relays.py` (`dev-docs/relays.md`).
- `channels/base.py` (`ChannelType`, `spawn_channel_task()`, `typing_keepalive()`, `log_id()`), `channels/router.py` (bot-enforced `allow_anonymous` / `allow_private` / `only_mention`).
